// A package that downloads data while it is installed declares it in its control file (Install-Download-Size, in bytes, and
// Install-Download-Source, an https address). apt tells the person which ones, with their size and source, right before it asks
// "Do you want to continue?", when the connection is metered (ORDER 399b; Daniel, 2026-11-04: "warn the user with current size").
// Stereo APTus reads the same declaration. The hook is /usr/lib/sparky-stereo-apt/install-downloads; it never stops an install.
AptCli::Hooks::Install:: "[ ! -x /usr/lib/sparky-stereo-apt/install-downloads ] || /usr/lib/sparky-stereo-apt/install-downloads";
// When it is shown: "metered" (NetworkManager says the connection is metered, yes or guess-yes; also when NetworkManager cannot be read,
// and that is said), "always", or "never".
Sparky::Install-Downloads::Announce "metered";
